+Change look gets a local Face detail toggle in its existing Face preview tools. The default remains the full 200 by 200 character. The detail viewBox is 36 75 128 110, symmetric about x100 so the existing whole-character mirror still reflects once. This gives at least 25/16 magnification and at most 20/11 depending on the SVG aspect ratio. Cropping peripheral ears, feet or clothing is intentional; full view remains one click away. Pressed state and the image label identify face detail.
+
+The toggle changes only viewBox and local state. It preserves the SVG and character node, sampled art, cheer start and original 1800 ms deadline, reduced motion, preview mood, unsaved draft and mirroring. It does not cheer, settle, save or scroll, and adds no clock, timer, listener or preference. Show preview retains instant scrolling and programmatic focus. Detail survives tabs, resizing and edits, and resets when the editor remounts. A third button uses the existing wrapping 44 px tool row.
+
+The initial 18 red unit cases all failed at the missing control; their exact source is archived. The first implementation passed 65 of 66 focused tests. One fixture switched to wide layout and then tried to click a narrow-only Face tab after remount. Removing that unnecessary click kept all reset assertions. After adding initial and live system/device reduction cases, the final focused run passes 69 tests in four files. No saved-field or look-model change was needed.
+
+The first combined native run passed 31 of 37 cases. Five new keyboard-focus assertions ran immediately after mouse selection, without entering keyboard modality. A distinct diagnosis retained the failure and recorded a focused, fitting 292 by 49 px Mirror button with focusVisible false. Entering keyboard modality with Tab fixes the setup. The first run also left one pending frame at a fixed later deadline sample based on a pre-click timestamp; the diagnostic rerun passed that case. The final test captures the actual native click time and each delivered RAF timestamp. It requires one pending frame before the original deadline and zero on the first delivered frame crossing it, within two 16 ms frames. The strict 1800 ms unit assertion remains. The distinct two-case clock run passed with event time 1049, pre-deadline frame 2848 and crossing frame 2864 ms, with zero pending frames. These harness corrections changed no product code.
+
+Adding conservative screen-stroke expansion to expression and glasses group bounds exposed a narrow-crop edge problem. That run passed 39 of 40 cases. The scruffy Bun group corner plus stroke exceeded the desktop crop edge by 4.206216 px. The product view widened from x40..160 to x36..164 while keeping y75..185. The same bounds assertions and tolerances remain. Narrow product/unit/native sources are archived, and happy, scruffy and unwell full/detail stills cover all species. This is a conservative group-box check rather than exact all-path painted geometry.
+
+The final native run passed all 40 cases in 91.395900715 seconds, with zero failures, cancellations or skips. Fourteen new cases run alongside 26 existing creator layout, motion and preview-tool cases. They cover all 15 species/mood combinations, unchanged SVG/art identity and markup, single mirroring, original cheer expiry, initial/live system and device reduction, actual cross-tab StorageEvent cancellation without replay, draft-only Save behavior and reset. Five enlarged-text layouts test 15 controls and focused visible art. All 29 final PNGs were directly viewed. Recorded desktop geometry has minimum conservative face stroke margin 8.61917274646596 px and maximum reflection/ground-y error 1.1368683772161603e-13 px across 120 paired points. All captures record their native Chromium version and method.
+
+Production typecheck, build and PWA generation passed after widening the crop. The full suite passed all 2558 tests in 137 files in 95.43 seconds. The final widened-crop focused run passed 69 tests in four files in 7.93 seconds. Strict lint and whitespace checks complete the final evidence before freezing. Heavy jobs remain sequential with capped heaps, one worker/browser and a 2 GiB run reserve; full launches require 4 GiB headroom. One bounded independent source/evidence/still review precedes a local checkpoint. This batch does not claim physical-device, assistive-technology, browser zoom or human temporal acceptance, exact continuous painted geometry, CPU/battery savings or process peak usage. Historical failed or partial captures are retained and excluded from final visual claims.
